WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.313
Step five builds the deployment
pieces from the registry,

2
00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:06.100
for the card management
revocation integration.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.100
It writes two files: the Logic App's
ARM resource, and the extension's body.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.830
Then set the Logic App's cloud to
one Learn gives no policy values for,

5
00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.688
build again, and put it back.

6
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:22.056
The second build exits one: Learn
documents the proof-of-possession

7
00:00:22.056 --> 00:00:25.488
policy only for Azure
commercial, so nothing is built.

8
00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:27.663
Step six checks the read-backs.

9
00:00:27.663 --> 00:00:32.051
The extension and the leaver workflow
both come back with no findings.

10
00:00:32.051 --> 00:00:34.481
Then move the custom task to the front of

11
00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:36.912
a copy of the workflow,
and check the copy.

12
00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:40.590
Two W X oh three findings:
Disable user account,

13
00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:45.526
and Revoke all refresh tokens,
don't run before the custom task.

14
00:00:45.526 --> 00:00:46.638
Block first.

15
00:00:46.638 --> 00:00:47.888
Exit code two.

16
00:00:47.888 --> 00:00:51.350
Step seven runs the tests: fifty-four, OK.

17
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.780
Step eight cleans up.
